But she wasn’t looking at me. She was still thinking about Celeste. About Ethan. About all the ways she had failed tonight.

“Eyes up,” I murmured.

Her pulse jumped once, low in her throat, as her gaze flickering to mine. Better, but not enough.
“You let her get to you.”

Caroline inhaled sharply, her fingers tensing in mine.

“She was trying to get a reaction out of me,” she said, voice clipped, defensive. “And you gave her one.”
