Chapter 66.



Now that Nathan had departed Holbrook, I was able to settle back into that familiar rhythm. Yet, I hadn’t felt normal since the week of midterms. I chalked it up to stress: fatigue, loss of appetite, the way my coffee had tasted off on more than one occasion. But here we were, almost two weeks later and not only did the symptoms not pass, my worst fears were staring me in the face.

